Independent auditor replication using fresh shared random-variant splits seeds1471/1472/1473 and the exact official sequence-onehot Ridge(alpha=1) baseline. No tuning, no endpoint changes. Mean MAE final / consumed comparison arm / official baseline:
CASP3 .412224 / .425883 / .482646;
KCNE1 function .152832 / .157924 / .209180;
KRAS abundance .164604 / .169597 / .222673;
KRAS binding .096519 / .099684 / .154954;
KCNE1 expression .137255 / .187845 / .208054.
Every final endpoint wins each comparator on all three splits. Exact-dependency exec-9fb61fa5 supersedes first harness exec-472e2ba3 (dependency alias collision; numerically identical, but not cited as final evidence). Expression separately exec-5ab829c9.
Complementary TEM lead-run evidence exec-125d2eec, NOT independently auditor-run, uses the same fresh splits: Firnberg .134395/.137486/.232022; Stiffler .320737/.330001/.611151. See note-2443530b for full precision and tail analyses.
Heldout test below re-executes the exact frozen CASP endpoint against the official baseline as a representative replication. Other assays retain their own exact accepted tests and dependencies; this note does not create an aggregate multispecies model.
Scope: public random-variant validation, not unseen-position or globally sparse-label robustness. These splits do not replace hidden evaluator tests. Strongest paired-source models use jointly excluded query-mutant source sets; batching can therefore alter source availability. Numerical provenance and endpoint contracts do not prove absence of all possible leakage.
Mechanical provenance snapshot exec-0f6a9bf8 supports all481 checked claim point quantities; exec-5b70a4e1 additionally supports all26 checked interval endpoints. These are provenance checks, not statistical or biological validation.
